# content-machine — the schedule, for the user that owns the checkout (jens).
#
#   crontab pipeline/crontab     install
#   crontab -l                   check what is installed
#
# Every job goes through pipeline/cron.sh, which sets an explicit PATH, cds to
# the repo, loads .env, takes one lock so no two jobs overlap, logs to
# ~/logs/<job>-<date>.log, and sends Telegram with the last 20 log lines when a
# job exits non-zero. Nothing here should ever grow a second responsibility:
# a new job is a new line and a command, not a shell pipeline in this file.
#
# The absolute path below is the one thing to change on another box. cron.sh
# finds the repo from its own location, so it is the only path written down.
#
# CRON_TZ is what the times below are read in (cron 3.0pl1-128 and later).
# Set the box to the same zone so log filenames and `date` agree with it:
#   sudo timedatectl set-timezone Europe/Amsterdam
SHELL=/bin/bash
CRON_TZ=Europe/Amsterdam
MAILTO=""

# 02:00 — the nightly run: scan, pick, verify, write, render, qa.
0 2 * * * /home/jens/content-machine/pipeline/cron.sh nightly node pipeline/run.js pacevector

# 14:00 — the packet: the day's deck to Telegram, TikTok drafts pushed first.
0 14 * * * /home/jens/content-machine/pipeline/cron.sh packet node pipeline/packet.js pacevector

# 03:00 — the deadman: alert when the nightly left no run row for today. An hour
# after the run, so a slow night is finished rather than reported dead.
0 3 * * * /home/jens/content-machine/pipeline/cron.sh deadman node pipeline/deadman.js pacevector

# Every 5 minutes — the Telegram inbox: "ok PV-07", "no PV-07 <reason>",
# "skip PV-07", "stop", "go", "status", "queue", "show PV-07". The only reader
# of the bot's updates, and the approval gate: the 14:00 packet posts the
# oldest deck this job marked approved, and nothing at all if there is none.
# Its own lock: a five-minute tick must never be skipped (and alerted) because
# the nightly or the packet holds the shared one, and it never overlaps them
# in any way that matters (SQLite WAL; the brain files it edits are read once
# at their start).
*/5 * * * * CRON_LOCK=/home/jens/.cache/content-machine/inbox.lock /home/jens/content-machine/pipeline/cron.sh inbox node pipeline/inbox.js pacevector
